  "he:Shabbat Evening/Shalom Alekhem:1": {
   "kind": "heading",
   "en": "Order for the Night of Shabbat"
  },
  "he:Shabbat Evening/Shalom Alekhem:2": {
   "kind": "heading",
   "en": "Shalom Aleichem"
  },
  "he:Shabbat Evening/Shalom Alekhem:3": {
   "kind": "instruction",
   "en": "This is the order of Kiddush based on the words of Rabbi Isaac Luria: After Maariv, enter your home. Upon entering the place of the table, say aloud and with great joy: 'Shabbat Shalom' and kiss the hands of your father and mother if they are alive. Then look at the light of the candles you blessed, and look at two candles, intending that one corresponds to 'Zachor' and one to 'Shamor'. Also intend that they correspond to the first Heh and the last Heh of the Tetragrammaton; although seven candles were lit for the honor of Shabbat, you should look only at two, intending that the upper candles shine. Then stand in the place where you sit at the table and say aloud: 'This is the meal of the King of the Jews.' Then circle the table to the right, and return to the place where you stood before the circling. Then, standing there, take in your hand two bundles of myrtle, one corresponding to 'Zachor' and one to 'Shamor', hold them and join them together as they grow between your two hands, bless over them 'Trees of spices' and smell them. After smelling, immediately, while they are still joined between your hands, say: 'Zachor and Shamor were said in one utterance,' and also say this verse: 'A pleasing fragrance to the Lord,' for in these words are hinted all the intentions of the blessing of the smell. Then circle the table a second time in silence while holding the myrtle. (Sha'ar HaKavanot, Shabbat, Beginning of Parshat Bereishit, 29).",
   "cite": "בא\"ח ש\"ב בראשית הכ\"ט"
  },
  "he:Shabbat Evening/Shalom Alekhem:4": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "<b>שָׁלוֹם</b> עֲלֵיכֶם מַלְאֲכֵי הַשָּׁרֵת מַלְאֲכֵי עֶלְיוֹן מֶֽלֶךְ מַלְכֵי הַמְּלָכִים הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא: ",
     "kind": "prayer",
     "repeat": 3
    },
    {
     "text": "<small>ג' פעמים</small> ",
     "kind": "instruction",
     "en": "3 times"
    }
   ]
  },
  "he:Shabbat Evening/Shalom Alekhem:5": {
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "<b>בּוֹאֲכֶם</b> לְשָׁלוֹם מַלְאֲכֵי הַשָּׁלוֹם מַלְאֲכֵי עֶלְיוֹן מֶֽלֶךְ מַלְכֵי הַמְּלָכִים הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא: ",
     "kind": "prayer",
     "repeat": 3
    },
    {
     "text": "<small>ג' פעמים</small> ",
     "kind": "instruction",
     "en": "3 times"
    }
   ]
  },
  "he:Shabbat Evening/Shalom Alekhem:6": {
   "parts": [
    {
